{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"restoring-shallow-blobfish","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Escaped-bug analysis (ticket cranial-goodly-seahog) found ~3 regressions where a guard/arg/behavior was added to one entry point and not mirrored to its siblings. Worst: halfwhite-chordal-stonefly ('--class requirement not propagated to MCP transition_ticket + NDJSON import') had 9 prior PASS reviews and ZERO findings. Also obnoxious-ogreish-neontetra, lemon-rabid-solenodon. Add a content-triggered surface-parity overlay: when a CLI command's args/guards/required-fields change, require the MCP tool + NDJSON/import path be updated in lockstep (or explicitly justify divergence). Advisory first.","id":"820d-6c54-412e-4470","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add code-review surface-parity criterion (CLI <-> MCP <-> import-format lockstep)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787070672257960001,"uuid":"c3ececa5-9b6f-44b3-9438-0f218f9d2378"}